WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.834
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 5, Network troubleshooting, which is 24 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:10.390
This lesson covers objective 5 point 5.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:15.765
Given a scenario, use the appropriate tool or protocol to solve networking issues.

00:00:15.765 --> 00:00:22.320
Today's concept: three commands that look alike, and which operating system and job each belongs to.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.597
Two jobs, two operating systems.

00:00:26.597 --> 00:00:30.030
The first job is showing your own IP address information.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.860
The second is tracing the path to another host.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.324
On modern Linux, ip addr shows the address.

00:00:36.324 --> 00:00:38.940
On Windows, the command is ipconfig.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.488
Linux still has the older ifconfig, but ip is the modern tool.

00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:47.540
For tracing, Linux uses traceroute and Windows uses tracert.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.865
So tracert is the wrong answer for a question about address information.

00:00:51.865 --> 00:00:53.738
It lists the routers along a path.

00:00:53.738 --> 00:00:55.610
It does not show your own address.

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:04.188
For the exam, to see IP address information on modern Linux, use IP space ADDR.

00:01:04.188 --> 00:01:05.520
Ipconfig is Windows.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.313
And tracert traces a path, it does not show your address.

00:01:09.313 --> 00:01:11.510
That's objective five point five.
